{"content":[{"c":["LIFE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["In biblical perspective, life flows from the living Father through the Son (his agent in creation and redemption) into a world thirsting for “real” life (see ",{"href":"?bref=John.6.57","r":"John.6.57","rawR":"John.6.57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.6.57","value":"John.6.57"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 6:57"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The Living Father"],"sourceClass":"h2","t":"p"},{"c":["God the Father is above all else “the living God” (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.10.10","r":"Jer.10.10","rawR":"Jer.10.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.10.10","value":"Jer.10.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 10:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.5.26","r":"John.5.26","rawR":"John.5.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.26","value":"John.5.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 5:26"},"). God, the source of all life (",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.6.13","r":"1Tim.6.13","rawR":"1Tim.6.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.6.13","value":"1Tim.6.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 6:13"},"), “inbreathed” humans at creation and sustains them continually (",{"href":"?bref=Job.34.14-15","r":"Job.34.14-15","rawR":"Job.34.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.34.14-15","value":"Job.34.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 34:14-15"},"). God alone gives life (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.17.16","r":"Gen.17.16","rawR":"Gen.17.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.17.16","value":"Gen.17.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 17:16"},") and takes it away (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.3.22-24","r":"Gen.3.22-24","rawR":"Gen.3.22-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.3.22-24","value":"Gen.3.22-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 3:22-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.6.3","r":"Gen.6.3","rawR":"Gen.6.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.6.3","value":"Gen.6.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.29","r":"Ps.104.29","rawR":"Ps.104.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.29","value":"Ps.104.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 104:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.12.20","r":"Luke.12.20","rawR":"Luke.12.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.12.20","value":"Luke.12.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 12:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The sign of life is movement; man is a “lively,” animated body (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.50","r":"Matt.27.50","rawR":"Matt.27.50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.50","value":"Matt.27.50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:50"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.8.55","r":"Luke.8.55","rawR":"Luke.8.55","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.8.55","value":"Luke.8.55"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 8:55"},"). Animals also have this animating “breath-soul” (Hebrew of ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.1.24","r":"Gen.1.24","rawR":"Gen.1.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.1.24","value":"Gen.1.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 1:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.6.17","r":"Gen.6.17","rawR":"Gen.6.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.6.17","value":"Gen.6.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:17"},"). Thus, all nature is instilled with life deriving from God (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.17.24-28","r":"Acts.17.24-28","rawR":"Acts.17.24-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.17.24-28","value":"Acts.17.24-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 17:24-28"},"). Life is therefore sacred, but unfortunately it is as transient as grass, clouds, dew, shadow (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.29.15","r":"1Chr.29.15","rawR":"1Chr.29.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.29.15","value":"1Chr.29.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 29:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.7.6,9","r":"Job.7.6,9","rawR":"Job.7.6,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.7.6,9","value":"Job.7.6,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 7:6, 9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jas.4.13-16","r":"Jas.4.13-16","rawR":"Jas.4.13-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.4.13-16","value":"Jas.4.13-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 4:13-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.1.24","r":"1Pet.1.24","rawR":"1Pet.1.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.1.24","value":"1Pet.1.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 1:24"},"). Long life is desired (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.29","r":"Gen.35.29","rawR":"Gen.35.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.29","value":"Gen.35.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:29"},"); any life is preferable to death and of infinite value (",{"href":"?bref=Eccl.9.4-6","r":"Eccl.9.4-6","rawR":"Eccl.9.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eccl.9.4-6","value":"Eccl.9.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eccl 9:4-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.6.25","r":"Matt.6.25","rawR":"Matt.6.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.6.25","value":"Matt.6.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 6:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.16.26","r":"Matt.16.26","rawR":"Matt.16.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.16.26","value":"Matt.16.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:26"},"), for Sheol houses a ghostly “nonliving life,” bereft of feeling, hope, or divine help (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.3-12","r":"Ps.88.3-12","rawR":"Ps.88.3-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.3-12","value":"Ps.88.3-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 88:3-12"},"). One’s life can be enhanced by loving and serving God (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.30.15-20","r":"Deut.30.15-20","rawR":"Deut.30.15-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.30.15-20","value":"Deut.30.15-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 30:15-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.3.8-12","r":"1Pet.3.8-12","rawR":"1Pet.3.8-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.3.8-12","value":"1Pet.3.8-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 3:8-12"},"), by experiencing God’s deliverance (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.38.16","r":"Isa.38.16","rawR":"Isa.38.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.38.16","value":"Isa.38.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 38:16"},"), and by receiving divine blessings (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.3-12","r":"Matt.5.3-12","rawR":"Matt.5.3-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.3-12","value":"Matt.5.3-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 5:3-12"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Christ as Life"],"sourceClass":"h2","t":"p"},{"c":["The Greek word for “life” is ",{"c":["zoe"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"},{"c":["."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," In classical Greek this word was used for life in general. There are a few examples of this meaning in the New Testament (see ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.17.25","r":"Acts.17.25","rawR":"Acts.17.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.17.25","value":"Acts.17.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 17:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jas.4.14","r":"Jas.4.14","rawR":"Jas.4.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.4.14","value":"Jas.4.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 4:14"},": ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.16.3","r":"Rev.16.3","rawR":"Rev.16.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.16.3","value":"Rev.16.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 16:3"},"), but in all other instances the word was used to designate the divine, eternal life—the life of God (",{"href":"?bref=Eph.4.18","r":"Eph.4.18","rawR":"Eph.4.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.4.18","value":"Eph.4.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 4:18"},"). This life resided in Christ, and he made it available to all who believe in him. Human beings are born with the natural life—called ",{"c":["psuche"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"}," in Greek (translated “soul,” “personality,” or “life”); they do not possess the eternal life. This life can be received only by believing in the one who possesses the ",{"c":["zoe"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"},{"c":["-life,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," namely, Jesus Christ."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The overflowing, vibrant quality of life made available in Christ was evident in the authority of his speech and the power of his touch (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.9.18","r":"Matt.9.18","rawR":"Matt.9.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.9.18","value":"Matt.9.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 9:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.27,41-42","r":"Mark.1.27,41-42","rawR":"Mark.1.27,41-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.27,41-42","value":"Mark.1.27,41-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:27, 41-42"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.27-29","r":"Mark.5.27-29","rawR":"Mark.5.27-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.27-29","value":"Mark.5.27-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:27-29"},"). He is “the author of life” (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.3.15","r":"Acts.3.15","rawR":"Acts.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.3.15","value":"Acts.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 3:15"},"), who provides the way into life (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.7.14","r":"Matt.7.14","rawR":"Matt.7.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.7.14","value":"Matt.7.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 7:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.25.46","r":"Matt.25.46","rawR":"Matt.25.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.25.46","value":"Matt.25.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:46"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.8.35-37","r":"Mark.8.35-37","rawR":"Mark.8.35-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.8.35-37","value":"Mark.8.35-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 8:35-37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.9.42-47","r":"Mark.9.42-47","rawR":"Mark.9.42-47","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.9.42-47","value":"Mark.9.42-47"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:42-47"},"). And he raised the dead with his life-giving power. His own resurrection made him “a life-giving spirit,” with the power of “an indestructible life” (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.8.2","r":"Rom.8.2","rawR":"Rom.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.8.2","value":"Rom.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 8:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.45","r":"1Cor.15.45","rawR":"1Cor.15.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.45","value":"1Cor.15.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.7.16","r":"Heb.7.16","rawR":"Heb.7.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.7.16","value":"Heb.7.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 7:16"},"). Thus, Jesus Christ is “our life” (",{"href":"?bref=Col.3.4","r":"Col.3.4","rawR":"Col.3.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.3.4","value":"Col.3.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 3:4"},")—in union with whom we find “newness of life” (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.6.4","r":"Rom.6.4","rawR":"Rom.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.6.4","value":"Rom.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 6:4"},") and are newly created, living henceforth not for ourselves but for him (",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.5.15-17","r":"2Cor.5.15-17","rawR":"2Cor.5.15-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.5.15-17","value":"2Cor.5.15-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 5:15-17"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["John, especially, dwells on the theme that Christ is the source of this new life (",{"href":"?bref=John.3.14-16","r":"John.3.14-16","rawR":"John.3.14-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.3.14-16","value":"John.3.14-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 3:14-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.5.21","r":"John.5.21","rawR":"John.5.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.21","value":"John.5.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:21"},") for the children of God (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.12","r":"John.1.12","rawR":"John.1.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.12","value":"John.1.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.3.3,5","r":"John.3.3,5","rawR":"John.3.3,5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.3.3,5","value":"John.3.3,5"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:3, 5"},"). This life is enjoyed already by those who know God and Christ (",{"href":"?bref=John.5.24","r":"John.5.24","rawR":"John.5.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.24","value":"John.5.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.17.3","r":"John.17.3","rawR":"John.17.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.17.3","value":"John.17.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Jn.5.11-12","r":"1Jn.5.11-12","rawR":"1Jn.5.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Jn.5.11-12","value":"1Jn.5.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Jn 5:11-12"},"), for they have already passed from death into eternal life (",{"href":"?bref=John.10.28","r":"John.10.28","rawR":"John.10.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.28","value":"John.10.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 10:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.26","r":"John.11.26","rawR":"John.11.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.26","value":"John.11.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:26"},"). Such life is abundant (",{"href":"?bref=John.10.10","r":"John.10.10","rawR":"John.10.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.10","value":"John.10.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:10"},"), enlightened (",{"href":"?bref=John.8.12","r":"John.8.12","rawR":"John.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.8.12","value":"John.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:12"},"), free and satisfied (",{"href":"?bref=John.10.9","r":"John.10.9","rawR":"John.10.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.9","value":"John.10.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:9"},"), victorious (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.6.6-14","r":"Rom.6.6-14","rawR":"Rom.6.6-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.6.6-14","value":"Rom.6.6-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 6:6-14"},"), full of peace and joy (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.5.1-11","r":"Rom.5.1-11","rawR":"Rom.5.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.5.1-11","value":"Rom.5.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 5:1-11"},"), inexhaustibly refreshed (",{"href":"?bref=John.4.13-14","r":"John.4.13-14","rawR":"John.4.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.4.13-14","value":"John.4.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 4:13-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.7.37-38","r":"John.7.37-38","rawR":"John.7.37-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.7.37-38","value":"John.7.37-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:37-38"},") and immortal (",{"href":"?bref=John.5.24","r":"John.5.24","rawR":"John.5.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.24","value":"John.5.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 5:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.51-57","r":"1Cor.15.51-57","rawR":"1Cor.15.51-57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.51-57","value":"1Cor.15.51-57"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:51-57"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["All this is possible because from the beginning “all that came to be was alive with his life” (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.4","r":"John.1.4","rawR":"John.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.4","value":"John.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 1:4"},", ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Thus, the life within the Father flows into the world through the Son, who also “has life in himself” and gives it to whom he will (",{"href":"?bref=John.5.26","r":"John.5.26","rawR":"John.5.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.26","value":"John.5.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:26"},"). He is “the resurrection and the life” (",{"href":"?bref=John.11.25","r":"John.11.25","rawR":"John.11.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.25","value":"John.11.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.14.6","r":"John.14.6","rawR":"John.14.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.14.6","value":"John.14.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:6"},") and demonstrates it by restoring life to paralyzed limbs, raising the dead, and conquering death (",{"href":"?bref=John.5.5-9","r":"John.5.5-9","rawR":"John.5.5-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.5-9","value":"John.5.5-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:5-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.43","r":"John.11.43","rawR":"John.11.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.43","value":"John.11.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:43"},"; ch ",{"href":"?bref=John.20.1-31","r":"John.20.1-31","rawR":"John.20.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.20.1-31","value":"John.20.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"20"},"). People remain in death only because they will not “come” and “have life” (",{"href":"?bref=John.5.40","r":"John.5.40","rawR":"John.5.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.40","value":"John.5.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:40"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Jn.3.14","r":"1Jn.3.14","rawR":"1Jn.3.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Jn.3.14","value":"1Jn.3.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Jn 3:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=EternalLife_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"EternalLife_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"EternalLife_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Eternal Life"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Life","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jn 6:57","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.6.57","rawQueryValue":"John.6.57","sourceRefExact":"John.6.57"},{"anchorText":"Jer 10:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.10.10","rawQueryValue":"Jer.10.10","sourceRefExact":"Jer.10.10"},{"anchorText":"Jn 5:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.5.26","rawQueryValue":"John.5.26","sourceRefExact":"John.5.26"},{"anchorText":"1 Tm 6:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Tim.6.13","rawQueryValue":"1Tim.6.13","sourceRefExact":"1Tim.6.13"},{"anchorText":"Jb 34:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.34.14-15","rawQueryValue":"Job.34.14-15","sourceRefExact":"Job.34.14-15"},{"anchorText":"Gn 17:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":